cff-version: 1.2.0
# This file describes one release, not the project's current state: `version` and the title's
# project name are the identity `v0.1.0` was published under, and neither is updated when the
# project moves on. Only the URLs follow the repository, which is where a reader has to land.
#
# v0.1.0 was frozen under the historical project name `jev-test`. The repository has since been
# renamed `jev-testbench`. No later version has been released.
message: >-
  If you cite this release, cite the tag v0.1.0. It is a frozen evidence set; `main` will move.
  v0.1.0 was frozen under the historical project name `jev-test`; the repository has since been
  renamed `jev-testbench`, and the URLs below follow it. The release itself is unchanged by that.
title: "jev-test: local evaluation bench and evidence freeze for TypeSafe Jev 1.13.0"
abstract: >-
  A measurement bench for TypeSafe's Jev model and the audit trail of what it measured:
  two frozen canonical logs (42 core records, 12 P3 records), a dated official-claims
  audit, a novelty triage, and a preregistered two-field experiment that returned a null.
  The scientific state at this release is NO_STRONG_JEV_SPECIFIC_NOVEL_FINDING_YET; the
  primary P3 verdict is P3_KILL_NO_SINGLE_FIELD_ATTRIBUTION. No general accuracy,
  calibration, latency, batching-ratio, determinism or production-safety claim is made.
type: software
